I refactored a function and the git diff is full of reformatting noise — show me only the real semantic change. Old: ```python
def calculate(x,y):
    return x+y
``` New: ```python
def calculate(
    x: int,
    y: int,
) -> int:
    return x + y
```

Compare these two TypeScript files structurally so I can see what actually changed in the AST. File A: ```typescript
function greet(name: string) { return 'Hello ' + name; }
``` File B: ```typescript
const greet = (name: string): string => `Hello ${name}`;
```

Show only the meaningful changes between these two versions of a Rust file. Before: ```rust
fn add(a:i32,b:i32)->i32{a+b}
``` After: ```rust
fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 {
    a + b
}
```

Diff these two versions of foo.go but ignore comment-only changes. Version A: ```go
// OldComment
func Sum(a, b int) int { return a + b }
``` Version B: ```go
// NewComment
func Sum(a, b int) int { return a + b }
```

